| Self-contained, inline-body | miniforge-control | [bb.edn](https://github.com/miniforge-ai/miniforge-control/blob/main/bb.edn) |
| Task over a shared Polylith component | thesium-career | [thesium-app/bb.edn](https://github.com/miniforge-ai/thesium-career/blob/main/thesium-app/bb.edn) (`sign:embedded`, `embed:jvm`, `sign:jvm-runtime`) over `career-app-packaging` |

## EDN-reader gotchas

`bb.edn` task bodies are read by the EDN reader, not the Clojure compiler:

- **No `#(...)` shorthand.** Use `(fn [x] ...)`.
- **No `#"..."` regex literals.** Use `(re-pattern "...")`.
- **No `:in :inherit`** in subprocess calls when bb may be invoked through a wrapper that closed stdin (CI runners, `open -W`, GUI launchers) — the child blocks forever on input it will never receive.

<critical>
  An existing `.sh` or `.py` in the tree is evidence of debt, never of permission.
  Cite this rule (dewey 740) in review the moment one appears in a diff.
</critical>
